# Jellyfin 10.11.11 environment schema (@env-spec / varlock format).
#
# The compose pins jellyfin/jellyfin:10.11.11, the newest STABLE release
# (2026-06-06). On 2026-09-03 (research date) the repo's `10.11.11`, `10.11`
# and `latest` tags all share digest sha256:aefb67e6a7ff1debdd…, and the repo
# is very much alive: 12.0-rc7 and nightly `unstable` builds were pushed to
# the SAME jellyfin/jellyfin repo on 2026-08-31. 12.0 is still release-
# candidate only (every v12.0-rc* GitHub release is flagged prerelease), so
# 10.11.11 stays the stable pin.
#
# BE HONEST ABOUT THE SURFACE: Jellyfin is a .NET server that configures
# itself from XML/JSON files under its config directory
# (system.xml, network.xml, encoding.xml, logging.json) and from the
# Administrator Dashboard in the web UI. Environment variables are a thin
# shim over that, and there is no env var for most of what an operator
# wants: the HTTP port, the base URL path, library paths, users,
# transcoding profiles and hardware acceleration are all dashboard/XML
# settings. Anything not listed below genuinely does not exist as an env
# var at this version; this file is deliberately short rather than padded.
#
# Source: the pinned image's own config blob (docker registry manifest for
# 10.11.11 → every ENV the image bakes in) plus a grep of
# `Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable(` across the v10.11.11 tree, which
# yields exactly seven names (JELLYFIN_DATA_DIR / CONFIG_DIR / CACHE_DIR /
# LOG_DIR / WEB_DIR / ENABLE_IIS / TRANSLITERATOR_ID) plus XDG_CACHE_HOME and
# XDG_RUNTIME_DIR. Everything else arrives through
# `.AddEnvironmentVariables("JELLYFIN_")` in Jellyfin.Server/Program.cs:346,
# which maps JELLYFIN_<Key> onto the ASP.NET configuration keys declared in
# MediaBrowser.Controller/Extensions/ConfigurationExtensions.cs (`__` becomes
# the `:` section separator; matching is case-insensitive). The defaults
# below are the literal values from Emby.Server.Implementations/
# ConfigurationOptions.cs, or the values the image bakes in.
#
# What the docs get wrong: the Configuration page's env-var example is
# `JELLYFIN_HttpListenerHost__DefaultRedirectPath`. There is no
# HttpListenerHost section at 10.11.11. DefaultRedirectKey is the bare
# "DefaultRedirectPath", so the variable that actually works is
# JELLYFIN_DefaultRedirectPath. That page's "Main Configuration Options"
# table also lists only 4 of the 13 configuration keys the code reads.
#
# NO PUID/PGID/UMASK: those belong to the LinuxServer.io image
# (lscr.io/linuxserver/jellyfin). This is the official Debian image whose
# ENTRYPOINT is /jellyfin/jellyfin directly, and there is no s6-overlay, no
# init wrapper, no user-remapping variables. Run it as another user with
# compose's `user:`.
#
# The compose sets exactly two variables: JELLYFIN_PublishedServerUrl (wired
# from the prompted JELLYFIN_URL) and TZ. Jellyfin needs nothing else filled
# in; it runs its setup wizard on first visit to the UI.

# @defaultSensitive=false @defaultRequired=infer
# @docs("Jellyfin server configuration reference", https://jellyfin.org/docs/general/administration/configuration/)
# ---

# ─── Core ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The public URL you open Jellyfin at, prompted at install. Feeds
# JELLYFIN_PublishedServerUrl below.
# @required @type=url
JELLYFIN_URL=

# The name the server actually reads; the compose passes JELLYFIN_URL
# through under it, so this is wired, not typed. Set JELLYFIN_URL. Maps to
# the PublishedServerUrl configuration key (AddressOverrideKey), which is the
# address Jellyfin advertises in its UDP auto-discovery replies and uses as
# the published base when the request itself doesn't reveal one. Empty falls
# back to the container's own primary IP, which clients outside the Docker
# network cannot reach.
# @required @type=url
# @docs("Container install: JELLYFIN_PublishedServerUrl", https://jellyfin.org/docs/general/installation/container/)
JELLYFIN_PublishedServerUrl=${JELLYFIN_URL}

# Timezone for the container. .NET reads it through glibc, so scheduled
# tasks, log timestamps and "recorded at" times follow it. The compose pins
# UTC; an IANA name like Europe/Berlin is the usual override.
TZ=UTC

# ─── Server paths (baked into the image) ─────────────────────────────────
# Resolution order per path is: command-line flag, then the variable below,
# then an XDG/HOME fallback (Jellyfin.Server/Helpers/StartupHelpers.cs).
# The image sets all five, and the compose's volumes are mounted to match:
# jellyfin-config at /config and jellyfin-cache at /cache. Changing one of
# these without moving the matching volume writes the data somewhere the
# volume does not cover, and it is lost on the next container replacement.

# Base data directory: the library database, plugins, metadata and the
# default parent of the config and log directories.
# @docs("Server paths", https://jellyfin.org/docs/general/administration/configuration/)
JELLYFIN_DATA_DIR=/config

# Directory holding system.xml, network.xml, encoding.xml and logging.json,
# the files that are Jellyfin's real configuration surface.
JELLYFIN_CONFIG_DIR=/config/config

# Transcoding scratch space, image cache and other disposable data. Backed by
# its own volume so it can be thrown away without touching the library.
JELLYFIN_CACHE_DIR=/cache

# Where jellyfin*.log is written.
JELLYFIN_LOG_DIR=/config/log

# Built jellyfin-web client assets served by the server. Only consulted when
# hostwebclient is true. Point it at another release only if you are serving
# a web client version deliberately mismatched from the server.
JELLYFIN_WEB_DIR=/jellyfin/jellyfin-web

# XDG fallback used to derive the cache directory when JELLYFIN_CACHE_DIR is
# unset (cache becomes $XDG_CACHE_HOME/jellyfin). The image sets it to /cache
# so the fallback lands on the same volume; ignored unless it is an absolute
# path.
XDG_CACHE_HOME=/cache

# Directory the Kestrel unix socket is created in when socket binding is on
# and no explicit path is given. Unset in this image, so the socket would
# fall back to the configuration directory.
XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=

# ─── Main configuration (JELLYFIN_ prefix → ASP.NET config keys) ─────────
# Every key here is read through .AddEnvironmentVariables("JELLYFIN_"), so
# the variable name is the configuration key with the prefix bolted on and
# `__` standing in for `:`. Values shown are the hard-coded defaults from
# ConfigurationOptions.DefaultConfiguration; the compose overrides none of
# them. NOTE: the listening port is NOT here. It lives in network.xml
# (InternalHttpPort, default 8096, which is the port this compose exposes)
# and is edited from Dashboard → Networking.

# Whether the server hosts the bundled web client. Set to False to run the
# API only, in which case the default redirect flips to the Swagger page.
# @type=boolean
# @docs("Configuring with environment variables (ASP.NET)", https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/fundamentals/configuration/#non-prefixed-environment-variables)
JELLYFIN_hostwebclient=True

# Where a request for `/` is redirected. The docs spell this
# JELLYFIN_HttpListenerHost__DefaultRedirectPath, which does nothing at this
# version; the configuration key is the bare DefaultRedirectPath.
JELLYFIN_DefaultRedirectPath=web/

# Whether the network manager subscribes to OS network-change events and
# rebuilds its interface list. Turn off on hosts whose virtual interfaces
# flap and send Jellyfin into repeated rebinds (this is what the
# --nodetectnetworkchange flag sets).
# @type=boolean
JELLYFIN_DetectNetworkChange=True

# SQLite page-cache size for the library database, in pages, passed straight
# to `PRAGMA cache_size`. Raising it trades RAM for fewer disk reads on large
# libraries.
# @type=number
JELLYFIN_sqlite__cacheSize=20000

# ─── FFmpeg ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Path to the ffmpeg binary, i.e. the `ffmpeg` configuration key
# (FfmpegPathKey). The prefix match is case-insensitive, which is why the
# image's uppercase spelling works. The image ships jellyfin-ffmpeg, the
# patched build every hardware-acceleration path expects; a stock system
# ffmpeg will fail validation or silently lose acceleration.
# @docs("Hardware acceleration", https://jellyfin.org/docs/general/administration/hardware-acceleration/)
JELLYFIN_FFMPEG=/usr/lib/jellyfin-ffmpeg/ffmpeg

# ffmpeg's `probesize` demuxer option for analysis. Raise it when Jellyfin
# misses streams in long or oddly-muxed files.
# @docs("FFmpeg format options", https://ffmpeg.org/ffmpeg-formats.html#Format-Options)
JELLYFIN_FFmpeg__probesize=1G

# ffmpeg's `analyzeduration` option, in microseconds unless suffixed.
JELLYFIN_FFmpeg__analyzeduration=200M

# Skips the startup check that the ffmpeg binary exists and reports the
# codecs Jellyfin needs. Only for a deliberately custom build that fails
# validation but works.
# @type=boolean
JELLYFIN_FFmpeg__novalidation=False

# Trades image-extraction (thumbnail/chapter image) accuracy for speed.
# @type=boolean
JELLYFIN_FFmpeg__imgExtractPerfTradeoff=False

# ─── Unix socket binding (Kestrel) ───────────────────────────────────────
# An alternative to the TCP port for a reverse proxy on the same host. This
# compose publishes container port 8096 instead, so leave this off: turning
# it on without also mounting the socket somewhere the proxy can read makes
# the service unreachable.

# @type=boolean
JELLYFIN_kestrel__socket=False
# Socket file path. Empty means $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/jellyfin.sock, or
# <config dir>/jellyfin.sock when XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is unset (it is, here).
JELLYFIN_kestrel__socketPath=
# Octal mode applied to the socket file after creation, e.g. 660.
JELLYFIN_kestrel__socketPermissions=

# ─── Miscellaneous ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ICU transliterator rule string used to fold titles into sortable ASCII
# (Jellyfin.Extensions/StringExtensions.cs). Empty keeps the built-in rule
# "Any-Latin; Latin-Ascii; Lower; NFD; [:Nonspacing Mark:] Remove;
# [:Punctuation:] Remove;". An invalid rule is caught and silently disables
# transliteration, so sorting quietly changes rather than erroring.
# @docs("ICU general transforms", https://unicode-org.github.io/icu/userguide/transforms/general/)
JELLYFIN_TRANSLITERATOR_ID=

# Hosts the server behind IIS. Windows-only and a no-op in this Linux
# container; declared because the code reads it (Program.cs:174).
# @type=boolean
JELLYFIN_ENABLE_IIS=

# ─── Image runtime (set by the image, not by the compose) ────────────────
# Baked into jellyfin/jellyfin:10.11.11. Not read by Jellyfin's own code;
# they configure the container around it. Listed so an operator who
# overrides one knows what they are displacing.

# The URL the image's own HEALTHCHECK curls. Change it in step with the
# server's port or base URL, or the container reports unhealthy while
# Jellyfin is fine.
# @type=url
HEALTHCHECK_URL=http://localhost:8096/health

# Preloads jemalloc for the server process; the image ships it because
# glibc malloc fragments badly under Jellyfin's transcode/scan allocation
# pattern. Clear it only when debugging an allocator-specific crash.
LD_PRELOAD=/usr/lib/jellyfin/libjemalloc.so.2

# glibc trim threshold in bytes, holding RSS down between scans.
# @type=number
MALLOC_TRIM_THRESHOLD_=131072

# Consumed by the NVIDIA container runtime, not by Jellyfin: which GPUs the
# container may see, and which driver libraries get mounted in. They have no
# effect unless the host is running that runtime, and hardware acceleration
# still has to be enabled in Dashboard → Playback.
# @docs("NVIDIA container runtime variables", https://docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/docker-specialized.html)
NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=all
NVIDIA_DRIVER_CAPABILITIES=compute,video,utility

# Locale for the container. Jellyfin's own UI language is a per-user setting
# in the dashboard; these only affect ffmpeg/shell output encoding.
LANG=en_US.UTF-8
LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8
LANGUAGE=en_US:en
